  "body": "# Gaoxy 0.12.2\n\nAn HTTP/1 peer that disconnects after sending request headers can now close\nnormally while Gaoxy creates the request exchange. Previously, a failed socket\nidentity lookup could raise `MatchError`, including for cancelled uploads with\n`request_timeout: :infinity`.\n\nExpected closed-socket errors stop the connection before application dispatch.\nAdmission ownership and retained bytes are released when the owner exits;\nunexpected transport errors retain their error disposition. Successful request\nmetadata and finite/infinite request deadlines keep their existing behavior.\n\nThe regression coverage includes controlled peer/local identity failures and\nsynchronized real TCP resets, followed by healthy sibling and new requests.\nAll six Hex distributions and the standalone application advance together to\n`0.12.2`. Dependency requirements and pins are unchanged.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-10-22T15:07:03Z",
